{"path":"ranges/iota_view/deduction_guides","title":"deduction guides for std::ranges::iota_view","titleHtml":"deduction guides for <code>std::ranges::iota_view</code>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/iota_view/deduction_guides","section":"ranges","kind":"page","summary":"This deduction guide is provided for iota_view to allow deduction from an initial value and a bounding value.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/ranges\">&lt;ranges&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> W, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Bound <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; requires <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*is-integer-like*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>W<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">||</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*is-integer-like*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Bound<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">||</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*is-signed-integer-like*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>W<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*is-signed-integer-like*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Bound<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><br>iota_view<span class=\"br0\">(</span> W, Bound <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> iota_view<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>W, Bound<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>This <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/class_template_argument_deduction\">deduction guide</a> is provided for <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iota_view\"><code>iota_view</code></a> to allow deduction from an initial value and a bounding value.\n</p><p>For the definitions of <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*is-integer-like*/</span></span> and <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*is-signed-integer-like*/</span></span>, see <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/is-integer-like\"><code><i>is-integer-like</i></code></a> ﻿.\n</p><p>Note that the guide protects itself against bugs arising from sign mismatch, like <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iota_view\"><span class=\"kw2932\">views::<span class=\"me2\">iota</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span>, v.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>, where <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code> is signed and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">v.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is unsigned.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cassert&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;ranges&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> io <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iota_view\"><span class=\"kw2931\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iota_view</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">1L</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">7L</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// deduces W and Bound as “long”</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/assert\"><span class=\"kw778\">assert</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>io.<span class=\"me1\">front</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1L</span> and io.<span class=\"me1\">back</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">6L</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"ranges","title":"Ranges library (since C++20)"},{"path":"ranges/iota_view","title":"std::ranges::views::iota, std::ranges::iota_view"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"deduction guides for std::ranges::iota_view","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. This deduction guide is provided for iota_view to allow deduction from an initial value and a bounding value."},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":105,"codeBlockCount":1}
